{"role":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — Google auth doesn’t change the access model.\n\nOn **cloud**, a matching sign-in domain only runs on **first user create**: it calls `addOrgMemberIfMissing` and does **not** add `project_member` rows. From there, project access is the same org-membership inheritance as a manual org invite (`getUserRoleInProject` falls back to the org role).\n\nOn **self-hosted**, Google signup also adds the user to the **default** project as a project member, plus the org — still the same inheritance for other org projects.\n\nSo with Google auth set up, joining the org is enough for project access. They won’t necessarily show up under Project → Team (that list is direct project members only)."}]}}
